EXPERIMENT 57 – LOAD TESTING FOR WEB-BASED EXAM SYSTEM USING APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to implement load testing for a web-based exam system.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Add HTTP Request Defaults and HTTP Cookie Manager.
4. Set:
   - Number of Threads: 50
   - Ramp-up Period: 25 seconds
   - Loop Count: 1
5. Add three HTTP Requests:
   - Student Login (POST)
   - Download Questions (GET)
   - Submit Answers (POST)
6. Add Response Assertion for status code 200.
7. Add Duration Assertion of 5000 milliseconds.
8. Add Summary Report and Aggregate Report.
9. Run the test and compare the 90% Line and Error % with acceptance criteria.
INPUT
Test Plan Configuration
Element	Property	Value
HTTP Request Defaults	Protocol	http
HTTP Request Defaults	Server	localhost
HTTP Request Defaults	Port	8080
Thread Group	Threads	50
Thread Group	Ramp-up	25 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Request 1	Method / Path	POST /exam/login
HTTP Request 2	Method / Path	GET /exam/questions?paper=CSA37
HTTP Request 3	Method / Path	POST /exam/submit
Response Assertion	Response Code	200
Duration Assertion	Duration	5000 ms

OUTPUT
Aggregate Report
Label	Samples	Average	90% Line	Error %
Student Login	50	<ms>	<ms>	0.00%
Get Questions	50	<ms>	<ms>	0.00%
Submit Answers	50	<ms>	<ms>	0.00%
TOTAL	150	<ms>	<ms>	0.00%

Acceptance criteria: Error % = 0 and 90% Line less than 5 seconds. Actual response times depend on the exam system.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to implement load testing for a web-based exam system, and the results were verified.
